# Scene / Inspector Authoring

Place tunable content in **scenes, prefabs, ScriptableObjects, and materials** — not spawned from code at runtime. Artists and designers must be able to edit values in the Inspector without reading C#.

## Prefer scene / asset authoring

- **Lights, reflection probes, post-processing volumes** — scene objects / volume profile assets, not `new GameObject(...).AddComponent<Light>()`.
- **Materials** — tune the `.mat` asset and prefab renderer settings; do not clone materials at runtime for the baseline look.
- **Grouping nodes, gizmo targets, spawn points** — scene objects.
- **Tunable numbers** (speeds, costs, timings, curves) — `[SerializeField]` fields or ScriptableObject configs, not hardcoded constants.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — light exists only at runtime; not editable in the scene
var go = new GameObject("RimLight");
go.AddComponent<Light>().intensity = 2.4f;

// ✅ GOOD — light lives in the scene; code holds a reference for reactive changes
[SerializeField] private Light _rimLight;
```

## When runtime setup is OK

- **Player/session objects** — spawned characters, cards, dynamic UI entries.
- **One-off bootstrap** for objects missing from every scene (`EventSystem`, audio managers) when no scene object exists yet.
- **Reactive state** — highlight emission, animated intensities, values driven by gameplay events. Runtime code adjusts values that must change with gameplay; the baseline is authored.

Even then, prefer a scene component with `[SerializeField]` refs wired in the Inspector over `Find` + `AddComponent` in `Start`.

## Runtime-created GPU resources

Any `new Material(...)`, mesh, or texture created at runtime must be destroyed in `OnDestroy` (or the static-reset hub if cached statically) — leaked instances hold GPU memory.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] New lights/probes/volume tweaks are scene/prefab/asset objects, not code-generated
- [ ] No runtime material cloning or `AddComponent<Light>` for baseline look
- [ ] Tunables exposed as `[SerializeField]` or SO fields, not hardcoded
- [ ] Runtime code only drives values that must change with gameplay
- [ ] Runtime-created Materials/Meshes destroyed on teardown
